<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>audio_url</code> is optional and short-lived. The API returns it only when private source-audio storage is configured.</p><p>Word timing is returned when the provider supplies valid alignment, including for Chinese text without spaces; incomplete timing keeps the original caption instead of inventing word boundaries. If <code>words</code> is absent, use the segment&#39;s <code>start_ms</code> and <code>end_ms</code>; do not calculate word timing by dividing a segment.</p><p>With <code>include_speakers=true</code>, segments can contain labels such as <code>speaker_1</code>, and <code>speakers</code> contains local display metadata. Labels apply only to that transcription, do not identify people across recordings, and ambiguous speech can be unassigned.</p><h2 id="retry-safely-with-idempotency" tabindex="-1">Retry safely with idempotency <a class="header-anchor" href="#retry-safely-with-idempotency" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Retry safely with idempotency&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Use a new UUID for different audio, language, or fields.</li><li>After an upload timeout, retry the same file and fields with the same UUID. The API identifies the existing job without processing or charging again. Even a completed POST replay is an acknowledgement; GET the result by ID.</li><li>Reusing a UUID with different audio or fields returns <code>409 idempotency_key_reused</code>.</li></ul><div class="language-json vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">json</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-dark github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{</span></span>
